save(k,t,dict(changes=cs,decisions=ds,inventory=ivs,notes='Manuscript page 6, pencil 12. The author returns to the isotopy category of anabelian oriented surfaces and calls its completion “compactifiée profinie”. He describes Hom spaces as locally compact, countable at infinity, totally disconnected and metrizable, with “toutes les qualités !” and adds “Et pas de pts isolés, par surcroît…”. This last blanket assertion needs a low-complexity exception: for the thrice-punctured sphere, self-coverings have degree one by Euler characteristic, and the isotopy classes of self-homeomorphisms form a finite group (trivial with individually fixed punctures, or S_3 if they may permute), so its completed self-Hom is finite and has isolated points. This is a mathematical note, not an alteration of the source. The second paragraph proposes a purely algebraic-geometric description independent of the complex topology. The first two field letters are plain C; the final one has the doubled stroke of blackboard C. Their common meaning does not justify normalizing their ink.',doubts=[],hand=[['Plain C versus doubled complex-field C','The first two field occurrences are single-stroke; the last has an inner stroke. This is local variability.','Both witnesses regularized the first occurrence; H also regularized the second.'],['disconnexes versus discontinus','The two distinct words occur in successive lines; the x in the second is clear.','H repeated discontinus.']],notation=[['Hom^wedge','The wedge is raised at the right of Hom; isot is a lower-right subscript in the second occurrence.'],['C / blackboard C','Both forms occur for the complex field on this page.']],abbreviations=[['compts','composantes, probably'],['pts','points'],['tjrs','toujours']],checks=[check('142-013-no-isolated','first paragraph, parenthesis','The completed Hom spaces have no isolated points without exception.','Refuted by X=Y the sphere with three punctures: a finite self-covering has degree 1 since chi(X)=-1, and the mapping-class set is finite. See refined statement 142-013-no-isolated-refined.',"refuted, with the refined statement's id"),check('142-013-no-isolated-refined','note on first paragraph','The no-isolated-points assertion requires an infinite, nondiscrete completed orbit; anabelianity alone is insufficient.','The finite self-Hom example above is a counterexample to the unqualified claim. No general replacement theorem is asserted.','targeted proof check'),check('142-013-algebraic-description','second paragraph','The completed category admits a purely algebraic-geometric description independent of the complex topology.','Read as the author’s announced construction, continuing on the next page; not independently proved in this event.','carried as background without fault found')]))
